ol probability. The wide generic-ballot margin may overstate the true environment slightly, so a modest haircut is applied while keeping uncertainty slightly above historical norms given the unusually large number of contested seats.", "key_factors": ["Generic ballot averaging D+8.4, a large midterm margin", "19 tossup House seats plus 29 Lean D and 26 Lean R races in play", "Multiple competitive Senate races across red and purple states", "Prediction markets broadly agree with quantitative estimates", "Late-campaign candidate volatility, including absences and debates"], "chambers": {"house": "Democrats are strong favorites for House control, with the generic ballot, seat projections and markets near 90 percent or higher all pointing to a majority in the low 240s.", "senate": "Democrats are favored for Senate control at roughly 60 to 75 percent, but a 49-to-55-seat range and competitive races in Texas, Georgia, Kansas and elsewhere keep Republican upside alive.", "governor": "Democrats are heavy favorites to hold a governorship majority, with a projected 28 seats and a 90 percent control probability."}, "environment_adjustment": -0.5, "uncertainty_multiplier": 1.1}}